  "$comment": "CV presets. Each names its sections, in order, and how each one selects items. `detail` chooses whether an item's `details` field renders — this is what replaced make_short.py stripping % SKIP markers out of the .tex. An item appears in a preset only if the preset name is in its `cvs` array AND it matches a section. A preset with `includeAll` ignores `cvs` entirely and takes every item that matches a section — that is what separates the complete CV from the curated `full` one. A section's heading is written once, in the complete preset's shape; a preset that shows fewer than every item a section could hold gets \"Select \" in front of it, worked out at render time rather than typed in.",
